WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.440
<b>Late April</b>

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.190
You two are warriors chosen to save Earth.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.400
Please lend us your power.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.650
We have to defeat the evil mage 
plotting to destroy Earth.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.510
Sounds like the setting of an old anime.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.620
All right! Leave it to us!

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.330
As a reward for your Knight's Pact, 
we can grant you each one wish.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.040
Hmm... Money, maybe?

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.760
No, cooking talent? No...

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.360
Take out the mage!

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.420
Is that an option?!

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.370
It's not.

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:36.260
If we could, we would!

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.770
<b>Episode 13: The Hero, Kusakabe Tarou</b>

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:40.050
What about making spring break last forever?

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:40.770
Impossible.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.660
There's a lot you can't do, huh?

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.700
By the way, that Hanako 
girl is odd, isn't she?

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.440
What makes you think that?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.280
The way her smile doesn't 
feel like a real smile.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:55.580
You're observant.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.340
Her emotions are subdued.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.650
She doesn't cry, doesn't get mad, 
doesn't get scared.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.310
So even her smile is subdued.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.110
She wasn't always like that.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.370
I see. That explains Kir.

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:10.130
Huh?

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.900
Kir's partners are always fearless.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:17.770
He's cold, scary, and I hate him.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.350
What about your partners?

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.850
They're cowards.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.010
What?!

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:28.310
Shouting back like that 
proves you're narrow-minded!

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.050
Einstein? Jobs?

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:35.830
I can't bring back the dead.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:37.400
Though injuries and illness I can heal.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.280
You just keep telling me 
you can't do things.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.110
Because you're making absurd requests.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.500
A wish, huh?

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:52.000
<i>That concludes our report 
on those enjoying the flower viewing.</i>

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.080
Thanks.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.000
Yeah.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.990
<i>The sight of so many 
enjoying the flower viewing</i>

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.710
Why are you eating here?

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.100
My parents are on a trip.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:59.050
<i>as they savor the falling of the late-blooming 
cherry blossoms was impressive.</i>

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.940
My parents both work, so they get home late.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.250
What a romantic setup.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.200
<i>The time for flower viewing 
will be coming to an end soon.</i>

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:03.600
Huh?! That's not how it is!

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.210
<i>Why not try going to see 
the flowers this weekend?</i>

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:05.680
We're more like siblings.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.890
<i>Now, our next story.</i>

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.610
<i>The criminal wanted 
for serial theft and murder</i>

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.110
<i>leapt from a building and killed himself.</i>

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.350
Oh, so it was true.

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:21.070
<i>The wanted serial murderer 
was discovered dead</i>

00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:17.500
Of course it was.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:18.470
What was?

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.380
I did that.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.450
<i>yesterday morning in Tokyo city.</i>

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.450
You did what?

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:29.290
<i>Investigation of the scene has led 
authorities to rule this an act of suicide.</i>

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.550
I saw the story on daytime TV, 
and thought he was an awful person,

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:30.000
so I killed him with my wish.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.630
<i>Police confirmed a note 
listing the murderer's motives,</i>

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:32.250
For real?

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.010
Hey, Kir Sonne!

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:36.370
<i>how he escaped police, 
and why he committed suicide.</i>

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:38.010
Did you properly explain it to Hanako?

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.340
Explain what?

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.020
That if you wish for the death of another,

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:44.390
the karma it brings increases 
the chance of your own death!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.070
I forgot.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.980
However, that's no reason 
to refuse a Knight's wish.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.310
You damn bastard!

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.400
Death is a constant 
companion in this battle.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.900
Screw you!

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.200
Come on, don't fight.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.910
It's all right, Lance.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.200
I'll be careful.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.450
Besides, if it does happen,

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.910
Well, I'm reaping what I've sown.

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.290
I see, that's your plan...

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.540
Can you do it?

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.460
Yeah, I can.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:22.370
It's possible to heal her the moment 
she receives lethal damage.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.230
However, there's one condition.

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:27.850
Condition?

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:32.440
She has to remain conscious 
when she receives the damage.

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:36.020
I can't save her if it's instant death.

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.900
You did mention that you 
can't bring back the dead.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:44.760
It's a great idea, but there's 
a risk it won't activate.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.120
So it's not a perfect trick.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.260
That's fine.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.830
I won't think of anything better.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.290
At the very least I can protect her 
with my body once!

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:00.580
N-No matter how scary our enemy is,

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.260
I c-can do it for her sake!

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:09.940
I don't understand what she's thinking, 
even though we've always been together,

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.390
but we've been together forever,

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.440
and I love her!

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:19.110
Manly, right, Lance Lumiere?

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.950
That's manly, Kusakabe Tarou!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:41.520
<i>When I looked up, 
that sky was full of wonders.</i>

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.690
<i>The despair I bottled up tormented me,</i>

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:50.640
<i>and I wanted the courage 
to break my chains of isolation.</i>

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.060
<i>(You are my light)</i>

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:57.650
<i>I was searching for your 
brilliant light in my hazy dreams</i>

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:01.940
<i>to kick away the limits placed on myself.</i>

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:06.910
<i>Now with your courage, 
let’s soar into the sky.</i>

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:09.450
<i>Let's CRUSH the fear!</i>

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:14.620
<i>I swear to you, at the ends 
of this chaotic world,</i>

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.370
<i>that even if you fall, I'll</i>

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.540
<i>Be the HERO!</i>

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:24.910
<i>I'll be waiting at the future 
we're moving toward,</i>

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:28.750
<i>with a “YES, MY LORD!” 
for your constant radiance,</i>

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.820
<i>clutching the stars raining down upon us.</i>

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:40.490
<i>I'll love you until we reach 
that future you want to destroy.</i>

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.420
It's strange, isn't it?

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.880
Hmm? What is?

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.590
We bathed together all the time 
when we were little,

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:20.500
so why do I now slap you 
when you catch me changing?

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.770
Why are you changing with 
your curtains wide open?!

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:24.490
Oops.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:25.860
Don't "oops" me!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:29.840
Good grief. This classic rom-com couple.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.950
Don't call us a rom-com!

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:35.540
I believe such surprise events 
are good no matter what era.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.900
I won't say the classics are bad, 
but you have to make progress.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:40.750
You two are annoying.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:43.450
Tarou-kun, hurry up a bit.

00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.710
We're going to be late.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.480
The snacks you make are the best.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.800
They go well with the booze.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.060
Hearing praise like that 
makes it worth cooking.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:04.940
Hanako's so used to my cooking 
she doesn't say anything anymore.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:07.820
Would a word or two really hurt?

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.280
Sounds like the problem 
of a long-married couple.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:13.240
Hey, listen to this. Just this morning—

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:19.910
And there you have it, a surprise 
event first thing in the morning.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.250
Outrageous.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.750
Outrageous.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.960
Give me a break.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.090
What do you mean outrageous?

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:29.300
You're not one to talk, Yuuhi.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.990
Huh? Really?

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.720
Brutus.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:35.230
She did see me fully nude.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.570
You were the one caught naked?

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:38.020
How nice.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.220
Is it really nice?

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.460
Oh, you're all together again.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.960
Oh, Princess.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:44.600
I came by to return a book.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.440
Huh? You borrowed one from me?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:51.420
I helped myself to one when I slept 
at your place the other day.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:53.460
You slept here?!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:56.140
Y-You slept over?!

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.290
You two are already that close?!

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.750
Huh? No, it's not—

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.930
Oh, i-it's not like that.

00:08:01.930 --> 00:08:05.330
Yuu-kun slept at my place during that time.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:06.780
You shocked me.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:09.380
Still, why did you guys do that?

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.560
Well, a lot was going on.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:14.670
That aside, it's getting hot in here.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:16.050
Shall I turn on the AC?

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:18.260
Why don't we go up?

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:20.970
Up?

00:08:22.670 --> 00:08:24.840
Ahh, nice breeze.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:26.810
This is great for sobering up.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.830
Wow, so high!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.670
Being up on a roof sure 
makes you feel young, huh?

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.120
Don't say it, it's embarrassing.

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.690
Y-Young...

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:38.670
Whoa, we're all acting young!

00:08:38.670 --> 00:08:40.330
This kind of thing is nice!

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:43.400
You say that because 
you're young, Kusakabe-kun.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:46.290
A man who carries his childhood 
girlfriend on his bike everyday

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.770
sure is different from the rest of us.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:49.840
She's not my girlfriend yet!

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.760
"Yet," meaning one day?

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.330
Hurry up and confess to her.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.360
Please stop that.

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:05.510
Hanako, let's go up to the roof sometime!

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:06.700
Using our Holding Fields!

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.400
No thanks. Sounds like a pain.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.040
What do you mean, sounds like a pain?

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:12.660
We're young!

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.360
It's fun!

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:18.420
I'm enjoying being young well enough.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:30.980
Oh, you were just pondering whether 
you should stay childhood friends

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:34.100
or confess and change 
your situation, right?!

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.390
You young bastard!

00:09:35.390 --> 00:09:36.440
Shut up!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.390
Think of it as taking 
a big step instead of flying.

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.520
Ow. I-I'll try one more time.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:47.930
If I can do this,

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:50.480
then I can stop Hanako when 
she does something reckless.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.350
Ow.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.950
I want to climb up on the roof again.

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.160
A golem?!

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:09.060
Now...

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:12.010
I wonder if everyone will be surprised.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.030
A Knight?!

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.560
What are those little ones?

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:32.980
Hm?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:35.860
Huh?

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.650
Nagumo-san and Shimaki-san are gone?

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:39.610
Subaru-chan and Yuki-chan, too!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:40.980
They've...

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:42.800
split us up!

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:43.780
Hey!

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.240
Where are you taking us?!

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:49.860
They took away all our main attackers!

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:04.760
What on earth are these?!

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:08.100
Maybe part of the ninth one? Or...

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.940
They're small targets 
and there's lots of them.

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:13.400
We're at a disadvantage 
with those of us here!

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:15.860
We have to do something 
to break through them!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:27.990
That golem has perfect offense 
and defense, plus it's strong!

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.330
I'll go around and draw its attention.

00:11:30.330 --> 00:11:31.710
Hey, wait, you idiot!

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.380
Then what should we do?

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.510
I'll do it.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.140
My Raging God will draw attention easier!

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:46.880
Huh?!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:48.470
Princess!

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:58.150
Holding Field! Raging—

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:06.840
<i>Hey, where the hell are you looking?!</i>

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.410
I love you.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:35.980
I know.

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:47.660
Raging God.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.210
Kusakabe-kun! Sorano-san!

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:06.960
Kir.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:10.220
I absolutely hate you.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.520
I don't want to see your face again.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:13.720
So.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:14.980
Lance.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.660
Don't you dare die.

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:33.630
Kir?

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:35.570
What's this?

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:38.040
Why am I...?

00:13:38.330 --> 00:13:39.800
There's no mistake.

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.660
It's thanks to Kusakabe Tarou and Lance.

00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:47.600
He used the wish from his Knight's Pact 
to heal you from a lethal wound.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:52.430
Why did he bother shielding you 
when he knew you'd be saved?

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:57.230
He died for nothing.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:02.980
Unstoppable Spear!

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:04.820
Mittwoch!

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.030
Drill Kick!

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.970
There're too many of them.

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:29.960
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:31.850
Your hero has arrived!

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:34.050
You all were in a pinch just now, right?

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.650
Right, right?! Ow!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.750
Why would you jump in 
when we're surrounded?!

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:40.600
Don't be so mad.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.020
Shinonome-san...

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:46.050
You all have done well.

00:14:46.050 --> 00:14:47.850
Now leave the rest

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:49.320
to me!

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.880
What are you planning?

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:56.250
You guys gather up into 
one spot and take cover.

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.590
He turned his Holding Field into spears?!

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.550
That's the Halberd Amamiya-kun used!

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:10.600
Aniki, this was your idea, wasn't it?

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.660
And it passed through Yuu-kun

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.430
to me!

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:18.270
Aerial Domain - Halberd Army!

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.960
A wide-area attack?

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:26.680
He altered the shape of that 
many Holding Fields at once?

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:28.860
He's crazy.

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.760
Ah, they ran away!

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:43.040
All right! Let's hurry back!

00:15:43.820 --> 00:15:45.460
Shinonome-san?!

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:49.630
That technique is crazy exhausting.

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:52.400
Mittwoch, carry him for us.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:54.970
Let's go!

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.170
Everyone, disperse.

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.620
I'll handle the rest from here.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.420
That's...

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:40.930
What the hell...

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:45.240
Goddammit!

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:55.750
Here.

00:16:56.090 --> 00:16:57.370
Thank you.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:18.640
Why do you keep drawing the same picture?

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:25.200
I thought I could get it out of my mind 
and get rid of it by doing this.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.960
You need not be afraid.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:30.760
You won't end up like that.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.120
Hyou-kun, you haven't shown 
any signs of grief for a while.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.700
Are you not sad?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.870
I am sad. Very much so.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.700
Nagumo-san didn't cry either.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:57.180
There wasn't any show of emotion as he 
called the police and took care of things.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.570
You two are both strong.

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:05.960
Kuh, there's no such thing 
as a strong person.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:10.310
I get a call from you out of the blue,

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:12.560
and it's to find out you're 
the first on the scene

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:14.050
to discover a corpse in the mountains?

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.320
Sorry.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:19.870
The deceased had your 
number in his cell phone,

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:22.320
but the higher-ups ordered that covered up.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:23.320
Higher-ups?

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:26.040
What do you mean?

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.530
I have a message for you from them.

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:33.520
"I'll take care of the small details 
so you can fight more easily.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:37.130
A game has to be fair, after all."

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.500
A game...

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:41.490
<i>So Animus did something?</i>

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:44.050
What's the meaning of all this?

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:46.770
I'm sorry.

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.100
A person is dead now!

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:52.610
What was your connection to 
Kusakabe Tarou in the first place?!

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.450
He was a comrade in arms.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.040
Ah, I'm beat.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:08.870
Ah, I'm hungry.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:11.670
Ah, I want a drink.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:13.000
Ah...

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:18.270
I want a drink with that guy's snacks.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:45.530
Hey, Hanako-chan.

00:19:45.530 --> 00:19:47.060
Oh, welcome home.

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:48.830
You're going to school already?

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.740
Huh? Oh...

00:19:51.460 --> 00:19:52.580
It's all right.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.040
You don't have to force yourself to smile.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.170
Take your time to deal with it.

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:04.270
Damn it.

00:20:04.270 --> 00:20:08.740
Why'd a good kid like Tarou have to die?

00:20:08.740 --> 00:20:10.890
Don't cry now.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:14.050
Hanako-chan's the one 
who wants to cry the most.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:25.500
Tarou must have used the wish 
from his Knight's Pact

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:30.620
to instantly heal Hanako 
if she suffered a fatal wound.

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:35.610
Yet he still leapt in to protect her anyway.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:40.450
Even though he knew Hanako 
wouldn't die from a single attack.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.220
He couldn't not protect her.

00:20:45.200 --> 00:20:46.960
Kusakabe Tarou...

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:49.280
He was a true hero.

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:53.680
A hero...

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.850
An image of someone strong...

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:59.800
The strength to protect others...

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:01.900
Neu,

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:07.520
I really want... to be stronger right now.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.270
You want power?

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:16.000
Anima?

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.330
I can't grant you strength of heart.

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:23.650
However, I can grant you power.

00:21:23.650 --> 00:21:24.970
Do you want it?

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:29.250
You'll give me power?

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.930
That depends on you.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:33.770
If you want it, then take my hand.

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:48.360
Princess? Hakudou-san?

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.240
Welcome, Yuu-kun.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.760
Amamiya-kun?

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:56.890
Amamiya Yuuhi, Hakudou Yayoi.

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:58.280
You two decide.

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:01.400
Decide which of you will become Invincible.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:04.120
<i>She's been crying...</i>

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:08.380
Of course we'll be fighting to decide it.

00:22:09.410 --> 00:22:11.600
We're both seeking power here.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.480
I want power.

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:16.770
The power...

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.760
to protect people and this planet!

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:25.690
Fighting to decide it? But Yuuhi's...

00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:28.340
I know you're strong, Amamiya-kun,

00:22:29.050 --> 00:22:31.030
but you don't need to hold back.

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:35.940
I'm fairly confident I can beat 
any human opponent.

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:40.570
All right. Let's do it.

00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:43.330
I want power, too.

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:27.480
<b>Next Episode:
The Knight, Sorano Hanako</b>
